# Component Access

## Cache component lookups

`GetComponent` walks the component list every call. Resolve once in `Awake` and cache.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — lookup every frame
private void Update()
{
    GetComponent<Rigidbody>().linearVelocity = _velocity;
}

// ✅ GOOD — cached in Awake
private Rigidbody _rigidbody;

private void Awake()
{
    _rigidbody = GetComponent<Rigidbody>();
}
```

## `TryGetComponent` over null-check pattern

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — allocates a "null" wrapper in editor, two-step
var health = other.GetComponent<Health>();
if (health != null) { health.Apply(dmg); }

// ✅ GOOD
if (other.TryGetComponent(out Health health))
{
    health.Apply(dmg);
}
```

## Banned lookup APIs in feature code

- `GameObject.Find` / `Transform.Find` for permanent wiring — use `[SerializeField]` references assigned in the Inspector.
- `FindObjectOfType` / `FindAnyObjectByType` per frame or per spawn — resolve once at load if truly needed.
- `SendMessage` / `BroadcastMessage` — string-based, reflection-backed, silent on typo. Call methods directly or use events.
- `gameObject.tag == "Player"` — allocates; use `CompareTag("Player")`.

## Serialized references

- Use `[SerializeField] private` fields, never `public` fields, for Inspector wiring:

```csharp
// ❌ BAD
public Transform muzzle;

// ✅ GOOD
[SerializeField] private Transform _muzzle;
```

- A required serialized ref left unassigned is a misconfiguration — fail fast (`Debug.LogError` or throw) rather than silently skipping (see fail-fast rule).

## Unity object lifetime

- Unity's `==` overload makes destroyed objects compare equal to null — but only through `UnityEngine.Object`-typed references. Do **not** store MonoBehaviours in interface-typed fields and null-check them; the check silently stops working.
- Don't use `?.` or `??` on `UnityEngine.Object` references — those operators bypass the lifetime check.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] All `GetComponent` results cached in `Awake`/`Start`, none in per-frame code
- [ ] `TryGetComponent` used for conditional component access
- [ ] No `Find`/`SendMessage`/`BroadcastMessage`; no `tag ==` (use `CompareTag`)
- [ ] Inspector wiring uses `[SerializeField] private`, not public fields
- [ ] No `?.`/`??` on `UnityEngine.Object` references
